answer.worked:
Rotate about the $y$-axis: $V=\pi\int x^2\,dy$. The region lies between $x=0$ and the left branch of the parabola.
$$\begin{align*}y&=(x-2)^2\\x-2&=\pm\sqrt{y}\\x&=2-\sqrt{y}\quad\text{(left branch, } 0\le x\le2\text{)}\end{align*}$$
The region runs from $y=0$ up to the $y$-intercept: $x=0$ gives $y=(0-2)^2=4$.
$$\begin{align*}V&=\pi\int_0^4(2-\sqrt{y})^2\,dy\\&=\pi\int_0^4\left(4-4\sqrt{y}+y\right)dy\\&=\pi\left[4y-\frac{8}{3}y^{3/2}+\frac{y^2}{2}\right]_0^4\\&=\pi\left(16-\frac{64}{3}+8\right)\\&=\frac{8\pi}{3}\ \text{cubic units}\end{align*}$$

