answer.worked:
The domain of $\cos^{-1}\left(\frac x2\right)$ needs $-1\le\frac x2\le1$, so $-2\le x\le2$. Since $0\le\cos^{-1}\left(\frac x2\right)\le\pi$, the range is $0\le y\le3\pi$.
$$\begin{aligned}x=-2&:\ y=3\pi\\x=-\sqrt3&:\ y=\frac{5\pi}{2}\\x=0&:\ y=\frac{3\pi}{2}\\x=\sqrt3&:\ y=\frac{\pi}{2}\\x=2&:\ y=0\end{aligned}$$
