\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Find the volume of concrete needed to make the sculpture.

answer.worked:
Rotate about the $y$-axis, so use horizontal slices with $V=\pi\int x^2\,dy$.

Outer surface $y=x^2$, so $x^2=y$ for $0\le y\le 2$. Cavity surface $y=x^2+1$, so $x^2=y-1$ for $1\le y\le 2$. The concrete is the outer volume minus the cavity volume.
$$\begin{align*}V&=\pi\int_0^2 y\,dy-\pi\int_1^2 (y-1)\,dy\\&=\pi\left[\frac{y^2}{2}\right]_0^2-\pi\left[\frac{y^2}{2}-y\right]_1^2\\&=2\pi-\pi\left(0-\left(-\frac12\right)\right)\\&=2\pi-\frac{\pi}{2}\\&=\frac{3\pi}{2}\ \text{m}^3\end{align*}$$

